          "description": "0-1 integer programming was the first in Karp's list of 21 NP-complete problems which was reducible to SAT. Pseudo-boolean constraints are another term for 0-1 integer linear programming (ILP). While ILP solvers also use exhaustive search (e.g. branch and bound) they make heavy use of relaxations of the problem. - wiki | IP solvers from the SAT perspective | Academic survey of Branch-and-bound algorithms\nSolvers include:",
